# reentry.xrs - the rung-3 gate: SequentialReentry produces two projection
# views with both eyes carrying the scene.
#
# Preconditions: the game in GAMEPLAY (the sewers save: title screen -> Return
# -> Return -> loading -> Return; the `[game] state` line must read GAMEPLAY, a
# menu or a loading screen drops the runtime to the quad by design), the sim
# session FOCUSED. The method arms on the first present after `stereo reentry`
# (the call-site patch lands at the next script dispatch) and needs a few
# seconds to pair up; the assertions read the composited eyes.
#
# Read with the log: `stereo: beat method=reentry out/s=N L/s=N/2 R/s=N/2`,
# `reentry: beat draws/s == 2nd/s`, and the pair line `the +1 present's c5 sits
# (0.0 ipd*scale 0.0) uu from the -1 present's`. eye-check.ps1 leg 0 is the
# pairing gate; its interocular bands are BioShock's (ENGINE_NOTES, "The
# scene-draw root": a true pair reads LOWER than the mono projection here).
reset
@mod stereo reentry
@frames 300
@assert sessionState eq FOCUSED
@assert projectionViews eq 2
@shot reentry
@assert capNonBlackL ge 30
@assert capNonBlackR ge 30
@mod stereo mono
@frames 60
@assert quadLayers ge 1
